# Coverage floor for lib/, enforced by script/coverage-check.
#
# A ratchet: raise these when coverage improves, never lower them to make a
# build pass. script/coverage-check reports when a criterion sits a whole point
# or more above its floor, which is the cue to raise it.
#
# Measured 2026-11-14 over 676 files in lib/, test files excluded, on the
# first CI coverage run that finished (2026-09-24: 88.7 and 93.3 over 402):
#   statement 95.5   subroutine 97.7   branch 79.8   condition 63.1
# The floors sit a few tenths below that to absorb run-to-run variation, not
# to leave room for regressions. Branch and condition coverage are reported
# but not yet gated.
statement 95.3
subroutine 97.5
